{
  "schemaVersion": "0.2.0",
  "kind": "graph",
  "title": "osf CLI replaces the two review-aid scripts",
  "summary": "The pr-lens workflow, and the pr-outline and show-me skills, used to edit a pull request description through two ad hoc scripts, one in Bash and one in Python. Both are retired. osf assets publish now pushes rendered SVGs to the orphan pr-lens branch, and osf pr section write now replaces one marked section of a description. osf pr section write also strips a link that wraps nothing but one <picture>, before it saves a section, because GitHub always renders a linked picture in light mode even in dark mode.",
